Fillets: 0940's surfaces unbounded through a trimmed surface, and their
curves in the period of the face (mitcad#1371).

The case: a key's top edge rounded with 2 over its narrow side, where the
key's end roundings meet the bore's wall, a torus (0940, mitcad#343). On a
body whose torus face lies on a Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface of the torus
(the replay's own, where the stored body has the torus itself), 0940 found
no run-on of the junction of the torus and the end rounding past their
vertex: ChFi3d_WideSurface gave the trimmed surface back as it was, and the
run-on's points past the trim projected onto it 48 mm off. The corners at
both ends then went to PerformIntersectionAtEnd, which failed ("Failed to
find edge"). With the run-on found, its curve on the torus, projected on
the torus itself, lay a period off the face's, and the torus faces came
out unorientable.

- ChFi3d_WideSurface: a Geom_RectangularTrimmedSurface is unbounded to its
  basis (the parameters are the basis's) before a B-spline is widened.
- ChFi3d_IntoPeriodOfFace: a face on a trimmed periodic surface takes its
  basis's period, so that a curve projected on the basis is shifted into
  the face's own range.

Before mitcad#1371 the case did not arise in the reported design: the item
before (a rounding past a concave corner tighter than its ball) fell back
to the file's stored body, whose torus is a plain torus. On the replay's
body before the item: valid, as on the stored body; before, the fillet
failed.

Upstream: new.
